   "date": "2020-12-08",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The speaker supported the Aged Care Amendment (Aged Care Recipient Classification) Bill 2020 but argued the aged care system is broken, citing the royal commission's findings of substandard care, and called for minimum staffing levels, transparency, and accountability of funding."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-400508",
   "speaker": "Ben Morton",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2020-12-08",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Aged Care Amendment (Aged Care Recipient Classification) Bill 2020 introduces a new assessment tool, the Australian National Aged Care Classification, to replace the outdated Aged Care Funding Instrument for classifying residential aged care recipients from 1 March 2021, without changing subsidy calculations, as a step toward responding to the Royal Commission into Aged Care Quality and Safety."
  }
